# F6, bicubic branch: a bicubic Patch's "P" carries sixteen vertex-class
# points (forty-eight floats), not bilinear's four -- RiPatchV derives the
# required count from the patch type, so a fix correct for bilinear can
# still be wrong here. This supplies two points; gman is expected to warn,
# clamp against forty-eight (not twelve) and keep going.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Patch "bicubic" "P" [-1 -1 0  1 -1 0]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 2 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
